    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0465" n="365" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg365"/>

                <head>No. 237.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Noyes to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 26, 1880</date>.
                        (Received July 14.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 361.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to State Department dispatch No.
                    239, of date June 2, 1880, I have the honor to inform you that on the 17th of
                    June I addressed a communication to the French minister for foreign affairs,
                    embodying the substance of my instructions as set out in said dispatch No.
                    239.</p>
                <p>I have received the reply of Mr. de Freycinet, a copy of which, together with a
                    translation of the same, I have the honor to inclose herewith.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EDWARD F. NOYES.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d237-a1.xml" xpointer="d237-a1"/>
            </div>
